     <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="rules_frame_layout">
      <item>
       <widget class="QLabel" name="rules_frame_label">
        <property name="font">
         <font>
          <bold>true</bold>
         </font>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Location replacements</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="LocationReplacementsEditor" name="rules_editor">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Each rule looks for its Text anywhere in a rendered location name and replaces it with Replace with. Check Regexp to match Text as a regular expression instead of a literal. Rules run in table order. Double-click a cell to edit it.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="WrappingLabel" name="rules_note_label">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Applied to a location name after its fields are filled in and before it is made into a valid filesystem name -- which is what lets a rule turn a separator like &quot;: &quot; or &quot;|&quot; into something the filesystem keeps, since sanitizing on its own would simply delete either. Rules run top to bottom, so a later one sees what an earlier one left behind. Text is matched literally unless Regexp is checked, in which case it is a regular expression (e.g. &quot; *\| *&quot; matches a pipe with any spaces around it) and Replace with may use its backreferences. A rule with no text, or a Regexp that does not parse, is shown in red and never applied.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="wordWrap">
         <bool>true</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <spacer name="bottom_spacer">
     <property name="orientation">
      <enum>Qt::Orientation::Vertical</enum>
     </property>
    </spacer>
   </item>
  </layout>
